\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Prayer is the soul's sincere desire,
\par Uttered or unexpresed,
\par The motion of a hidden fire
\par That trembles in the breast.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Prayer is the burden of a sign,
\par The falling of a tear,
\par The upward glancing of an eye
\par When none but God is near.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Prayer is the simplest form of speech
\par That infant lips can try;
\par Prayer the sublimest strains that reach
\par The majesty on high.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Prayer is the contrite sinner's voice
\par Returning from His ways,
\par While angels in their songs rejoice,
\par And cry: Behold he prays!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Prayer is the Christian's vital breath,
\par The Christians native air,
\par His watchword at the gates of death;
\par He enters heaven with prayer.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. O Thou by whom we come to God,
\par The Life, the Truth, the Way!
\par The path of prayer Thyself hast trod:
\par Lord! teach us how to pray.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

